 ## Background
-The method is derived from the voxel ocean simulation codebase, specifically the neighbor search logic used for fluid or particle interactions [S1, unofficial]. It is part of a larger system that includes voxelization, marching, and rendering configurations [S1, unofficial]. The implementation uses a clamped bounding box approach to efficiently limit the search space to a sphere, avoiding the need for more complex spatial partitioning structures like KD-trees or octrees for small-scale searches.
